WEBVTT

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:27.110
SHUNSUKE SENGOKU

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:31.710
From deep within the darkest
corners of the night,

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:35.790
Oh, we're gonna take the
answer; make, make me down.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:36.710
MERRILL YANAGAWA

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:38.470
Oh, we're gonna take the
answer; make, make me down.

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:44.310
I hear a voice I cannot,
no, will not forget.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.180
GABIMARU RIKIYA

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:49.230
I'm running away from flash
lights; what, what is wrong?

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:56.380
Once there was a dark night,

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:59.870
When we loved each other,

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:04.670
So desperate, yet so sad,

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:10.140
Never to return.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:14.220
Lonely game, silly game,

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:17.790
There can be no retreat
from night and day!

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:19.390
Endless game,

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:24.140
Hold on tightly
to your broken dreams.

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:27.550
Follow me, stay with me,

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:30.950
Last chance,
time to risk it all!

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:34.990
It's so hard,

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:38.500
Baby, let me go.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:40.540
Just Burning World!

00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:03.420
The Decoy Program

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.390
Do you really think you
can get it off, Yamabana?

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:57.390
Dunno. They used seven fuses,
and I've already removed four of them.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:02.790
You only have 15 minutes left
before your timer detonates.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.190
Don't rush me.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:08.790
Did Hasegawa send you
to track me down?

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:12.070
Yeah.
It's a rotten job.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:17.870
You found me. Even if I get
my collar off, I'm still trapped.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:24.110
Not at all. Once your collar's off,
you can start on mine.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.670
Next, the one on the right.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:38.190
Just two more.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:42.670
I heard you sold Cyber Police
files on the black market.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:46.300
I knew it would cost me my neck,
but they paid millions.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.000
Who did?

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.560
I can't tell you that.
I still have some pride.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:54.510
Which fuse should I take out next?

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:56.870
The one on the right.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:58.950
No, I think it's the left.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.420
RECORD PURGED
He wouldn't tell you
where he sold the files?

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:34.420
No. But you have a
pretty good idea, don't you?

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:38.150
Whoever it was,
they paid a bundle for that file.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:40.510
Hardly our usual brand of cheap thug.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.360
They're going to slip up.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:52.590
very soon.
And I'll be ready.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:21.780
Stay back!

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:30.620
It's a monster!

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:51.270
victim identified as
James Takagi, age 32.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:55.790
Six prior convictions;
suspected in a recent robbery.

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:59.870
Whatever he did,
it's a rotten way to go.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.110
varsus, take a look at this.

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:14.270
A protection suit?

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:17.400
This model is only used
by Special Forces.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:18.350
The army?

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.590
You shouldn't have tried
this in broad daylight.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:40.150
Trafficking in body parts.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:46.270
I don't suppose you'll
come along quietly?

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:10.910
That's a pretty big order.
Who's the customer?

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:15.550
Or maybe you don't mind trading
some parts of your own?

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:19.070
Wait, I'll talk!

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:20.880
IDENTITY CHECK: *SHIRO*
I found him, Benten.

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:26.150
Kazuo Shiroyama,
30 years old.

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:29.270
He works for the
army's Special Forces.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:31.970
Special Forces?
A formidable enemy.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:36.770
What a coincidence. Sengoku
just got blueprints to their base.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:37.730
He did?

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:42.530
I think his latest case involves
the Special Forces, somehow.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:47.170
It is illegal to trespass
on military property.

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:48.210
Sure is.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:53.050
But they aren't going to give us
a warrant without better proof.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:55.810
This action is not sanctioned.

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:58.010
Give it a rest.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:03.810
This unit functions 24 hours per day.
Inactivity is not required.

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:07.050
Get lost.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:11.490
This unit is equipped with
a Global Positioning System.

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:16.090
Coordinates are continually
updated. Order impossible.

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:19.090
No such idiom is listed
in the speech tables.

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:25.850
Searching linguistic database
for a phrase correlation.

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:56.120
Boy oh boy.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:04.250
Forget it. The gates are
synchronized to the tide.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:06.730
They won't open until low tide.

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:11.620
Oh, wonderful. Are you here to
clean out the army's sewers?

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:13.050
Something like that.

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:16.770
The gates won't open
for another six hours.

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:19.770
I should have brought
a deck of cards.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.330
Give me a hand.
These might come in handy later.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:35.450
Do it yourself.
I'm going to take a nap.

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:12.190
Keep it down. I hate to be
interrupted while I'm reading.

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:15.390
Army, Special Forces.
We need to search your vehicle.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:18.230
For what reason?

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:21.790
We're in pursuit of a
cyber criminal, a female.

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:23.470
We lost her near this area.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:29.950
A cyber criminal?
Maybe I should give you a hand.

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:36.060
A Cyber Cop? Have you seen
a young woman in the area?

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:40.230
No. But I'll let
you know if I see her.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:43.310
Be sure you do.

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:46.430
It checks out, here.

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:01.790
So, Sara, how'd you get
Special Forces so mad at you?

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:11.700
You saved me.

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:17.550
It's been a while.

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:19.510
You haven't changed a bit.

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:21.230
Yeah, right.

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:26.030
But the work's been
sour, ever since we split up.

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:30.190
None of my jobs have gone right.
Let's work together again.

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:34.270
Cut it out. These days I'm
busy catching cyber criminals.

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:37.110
At least until this collar comes off.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:41.790
I was kidding.
I know you're a cop now.

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:45.830
How'd you get
Special Forces so upset?

00:11:46.840 --> 00:11:49.220
I hacked into their
tactical computer.

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:51.910
I was hoping to find
something I could sell.

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:55.150
This.

00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:59.630
But then they caught me.
Sucks.

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:05.830
I got the data, but I couldn't
find the decryption code.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:21.230
Incredible!
You've already cracked it!

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:30.190
Goggles, you really ARE a genius!

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:31.620
Don't flatter me.

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:36.790
Top secret...

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:44.630
Bad news.
You stumbled onto something big.

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:48.270
They're coming back!

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:51.510
What are you doing?

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:30.630
You stole their biggest secret.
They can't let you escape.

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:33.740
They'd just love it
if you wound up dead.

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:52.910
This is Iron-70. The prey is
heading north, to sector 4-RJ.

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:56.470
very well.
Give them some rope.

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:57.710
Roger.

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:03.840
We haven't heard from
Sengoku or Benten for 4 hours!

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:08.190
I know where they are.
We can't risk sending a signal in.

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:09.710
But...

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:13.150
That will be all, Miss Jonouchi.

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:21.030
Hasegawa.

00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:25.190
Well, if it isn't Chief
Advisor Mashiba. Long time.

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:29.830
How are the Cyber Police
doing these days?

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:33.720
I didn't know you
cared about the police,

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:36.310
or the dull work
of keeping the peace.

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:38.030
A soldier always
cares about peace.

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:42.790
For example, Oedo seems
to be in deep trouble.

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:49.910
Every year, the crime rate increases.
I'm very concerned.

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:52.030
I'm sure.

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:59.550
But I didn't call just to tell you
my opinion. I have business.

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:01.270
I'm listening.

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:08.750
Data has been stolen from
our most restricted computer.

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:11.440
The criminal is a Cyber
Policeman I believe,

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:14.790
code-named "Goggles."

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:19.270
I believe he's one of your "hounds."

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:22.000
He used to be a criminal, didn't he?

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:24.870
It's only natural that he'd
return to his criminal ways.

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:28.070
Don't worry. I'll take care of...

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:30.780
We'd prefer to handle this ourselves.

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:35.510
Since this involves top secret data,
the police can't interfere.

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:39.070
Besides, we have a weapon that's
perfect for this situation.

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:40.780
A weapon?

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:42.950
Let me tell you about it.

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:48.670
It was invented for policing
operations, just like this one.

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:52.390
How ironic that we'll be using
it against a Cyber Policeman.

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:59.300
But this WILL provide a perfect
test of the weapon's abilities.

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:04.950
I'll give a record of
this test to the President.

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:07.000
I'm sure he'll be very interested.

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:10.700
He might even ask us to
take over all police work in Oedo.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:12.910
That's a lovely little story.

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:18.590
Then you wouldn't have to work
so hard controlling your hounds.

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:23.390
We'd put them back in
prison where they belong.

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:30.030
Interesting. But my hounds
have fangs; very sharp fangs.

00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:35.060
I hope your new weapon has
been immunized against rabies.

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:40.430
You'll find out soon
enough, Hasegawa.

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:44.590
You can start working
on your retirement plans.

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:46.700
Mashiba, out.

00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:50.990
How did it go, sir?

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:52.150
Exactly as planned.

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:55.590
Don't disappoint me,
Major Shiroyama.

00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:59.150
Don't worry, sir.
MOLCOS is ready to go.

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:24.320
Hasegawa here.

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:30.020
Can't this wait?
I'm on a date.

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:31.810
I know the military
is chasing you.

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:35.970
Goggles, what's
their new weapon?

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:39.050
Answer me.

00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:41.690
The top secret data?

00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:43.090
Yes.

00:17:43.980 --> 00:17:47.250
I'm not sure. It looks
like some kind of cyborg.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:50.810
Goggles, I want you to fight it.

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:52.890
What?

00:17:53.620 --> 00:17:55.370
There's no time to explain.

00:17:55.780 --> 00:17:59.930
They're going to attack you with it,
but you have to beat it.

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:03.690
That's an order.
I'm setting your timer.

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:06.890
You have 8 hours to
destroy their new weapon.

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:09.850
We aren't your damned puppets!

00:18:10.700 --> 00:18:11.610
Goggles!

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:15.810
Don't worry, I'll protect you.

00:18:36.940 --> 00:18:39.610
We're forcing them in
your direction. Get ready.

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:42.730
Roger. Keep the pressure up.

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:48.770
Hold on tight!

00:19:18.580 --> 00:19:19.800
Are you all right?

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:22.010
You're so insane sometimes!

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:26.690
It's a nice change to be chased
again, rather than chasing.

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:29.270
It almost feels like old times.

00:19:39.290 --> 00:19:41.750
Yeah, it does feel like old times.

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:47.960
Remember when we hacked
into that satellite?

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:50.840
That was fun.

00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:56.870
Those were the days.
I wish we could go back.

00:19:59.610 --> 00:20:01.910
I don't care!
Shoot the woman!

00:20:07.210 --> 00:20:09.080
Damn you!

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:22.600
Good shot.
You haven't changed a bit.

00:20:26.690 --> 00:20:31.400
That's not true. I've changed.
I've changed a lot.

00:20:33.570 --> 00:20:34.880
Wake up, Sengoku.

00:21:01.050 --> 00:21:02.760
varsus, do you read me?

00:21:03.250 --> 00:21:04.640
Affirmative.

00:21:04.730 --> 00:21:08.560
I'm sending a picture.
Does it match the print we saw before?

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:10.360
Lmage received.

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:20.240
Complete.

00:21:20.530 --> 00:21:23.720
Perfect correlation with the
print from the crime scene.

00:21:39.810 --> 00:21:41.800
A rather gruesome hobby.

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:43.320
Hey, Benten!

00:21:46.050 --> 00:21:46.730
Look at this!

00:21:49.770 --> 00:21:51.050
I don't know.

00:21:52.210 --> 00:21:54.400
Maybe he's joining the army.

00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:55.640
It can't be!

00:21:56.130 --> 00:21:59.400
It's a battle simulation.
Goggles against... a new weapon?

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:04.160
They're going to test their
new weapon against Goggles.

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:07.440
They've picked him to
be their guinea pig.

00:22:12.770 --> 00:22:15.520
Goggles, pull over.

00:22:34.170 --> 00:22:35.840
What's wrong, Sara?

00:22:42.130 --> 00:22:43.560
I lied to you.

00:22:44.810 --> 00:22:47.840
This was just a trap
to lure you out here.

00:22:50.890 --> 00:22:56.680
Last month, I found a password
to a Special Forces computer.

00:22:57.570 --> 00:23:01.680
I knew the risks, but the
payoff could have been huge.

00:23:02.810 --> 00:23:05.720
But it was an ambush,
and Special Forces caught me.

00:23:06.810 --> 00:23:11.320
They offered me freedom
if I'd sell out an old friend.

00:23:11.810 --> 00:23:13.240
So go ahead and shoot me.

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:16.760
I only have 8 hours anyway,
before my collar explodes.

00:23:21.010 --> 00:23:26.030
You know I can't do that.
What's happened to me?

00:23:26.810 --> 00:23:29.680
You were trapped
as much as I was.

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:33.200
Once you've fulfilled your side
of the bargain, they'll kill you.

00:23:34.410 --> 00:23:37.600
I'm pathetic.
I hate myself.

00:23:41.690 --> 00:23:48.160
I didn't know it would come to this,
but I can't take it back.

00:23:48.570 --> 00:23:51.640
Everyone makes mistakes.
Forget it.

00:23:57.010 --> 00:24:00.200
You were my best partner.

00:24:00.610 --> 00:24:06.200
Someday, I'll get this collar off
and we can team up again.

00:24:07.610 --> 00:24:11.600
And this time they won't
be able to catch me.

00:24:21.730 --> 00:24:27.600
That's the new weapon?
Sara, get out of here. He's after me.

00:24:31.170 --> 00:24:32.040
Sara!

00:24:38.370 --> 00:24:39.350
I don't...

00:24:47.170 --> 00:24:49.520
Don't, Sara!

00:24:50.450 --> 00:24:55.240
I don't deserve to be
your partner any more!

00:26:29.900 --> 00:26:34.090
You're under arrest as
a felony accomplice.

00:26:35.740 --> 00:26:39.490
I see she's dead.
What a fool.

00:26:39.940 --> 00:26:45.130
You bastard!
You lured Sara into this.

00:26:46.340 --> 00:26:49.960
Small loss.
She was no longer necessary.

00:26:50.620 --> 00:26:55.090
But we still need you for one more task.
Come with us.

00:26:59.190 --> 00:27:01.380
It's a psychic amplification suit.

00:27:01.990 --> 00:27:06.980
It stimulates the brain core,
to enhance esper abilities.

00:27:07.990 --> 00:27:09.540
Esper abilities?

00:27:10.190 --> 00:27:14.940
They're using butchered corpses
to make psychic cyborgs?

00:27:15.630 --> 00:27:16.770
That's what it looks like.

00:27:17.870 --> 00:27:21.300
There's no way Goggles
can beat a monster like that.

00:27:21.510 --> 00:27:22.700
Not likely.

00:27:23.270 --> 00:27:27.420
We'll know for sure, once we
conduct the weapons test.

00:27:28.030 --> 00:27:30.780
But you won't live to see that.

00:27:36.590 --> 00:27:39.020
This should take care of you.

00:27:39.590 --> 00:27:42.220
It isn't the most elegant way to die.

00:27:42.830 --> 00:27:45.130
It's good enough
for a mangy hound.

00:27:45.590 --> 00:27:48.260
Get in there...
show me you've got some guts!

00:27:50.790 --> 00:27:53.500
Backup power comes
up in three seconds.

00:27:53.630 --> 00:27:55.540
Plenty of time.

00:27:58.030 --> 00:28:01.020
Good dogs.

00:28:24.470 --> 00:28:27.030
Start talking, or we
put you in the press.

00:28:27.710 --> 00:28:29.900
Where's the weapons test?

00:28:40.990 --> 00:28:41.940
Get out!

00:28:49.590 --> 00:28:50.940
very considerate.

00:29:13.430 --> 00:29:15.340
Time for the main event.

00:29:36.110 --> 00:29:39.220
I finally figured it out.

00:29:40.350 --> 00:29:44.300
YOU bought the Cyber Police
files from Yamabana.

00:29:44.910 --> 00:29:48.690
Those files listed Sara as
one of my former partners.

00:29:49.110 --> 00:29:51.670
So you used her as a lure,
to suck me into your trap.

00:29:53.270 --> 00:29:58.340
All of this is just to
test that monster of yours.

00:30:03.750 --> 00:30:05.820
So how should you
bet on this match?

00:30:06.270 --> 00:30:08.140
The smart money's on me.

00:30:08.870 --> 00:30:11.940
Your champion is going to take a fall.

00:30:14.390 --> 00:30:14.980
Begin.

00:30:30.590 --> 00:30:31.260
Let's do it.

00:30:55.390 --> 00:30:58.540
There's no way I can
beat him in close combat.

00:31:21.190 --> 00:31:22.140
Take this!

00:31:30.390 --> 00:31:31.220
Damn!

00:31:31.990 --> 00:31:33.050
Magnificent!

00:31:33.190 --> 00:31:37.500
This is the finest ground-assault
unit I've ever seen!

00:31:37.630 --> 00:31:42.020
The brain stimulation routines
have barely started.

00:31:42.150 --> 00:31:46.140
Our guinea pig may not survive
to see MOLCOS reach full power.

00:32:29.070 --> 00:32:31.700
Power output in
MOLCOS is rising rapidly.

00:32:35.430 --> 00:32:38.820
Temperature is at 120 degrees.
The pumps are compensating.

00:32:41.510 --> 00:32:42.980
His powers are awakening.

00:33:05.430 --> 00:33:07.580
MOLCOS is magnificent.

00:33:07.710 --> 00:33:09.900
This is a splendid test.

00:33:10.030 --> 00:33:11.540
Thank you, sir.

00:33:11.670 --> 00:33:14.820
MOLCOS, it's time to finish him off.

00:33:34.550 --> 00:33:36.700
Glad you dropped by!

00:33:40.550 --> 00:33:41.770
What's going on?

00:33:42.230 --> 00:33:43.580
It's an army floater!

00:33:43.950 --> 00:33:45.660
Who's piloting?

00:33:47.030 --> 00:33:48.540
My men.

00:33:49.790 --> 00:33:50.740
Hasegawa!

00:33:53.670 --> 00:33:55.220
Let him through.

00:33:59.270 --> 00:34:04.020
Mashiba, I have enough evidence
to close this operation down.

00:34:04.390 --> 00:34:09.820
Your weapon is guilty of murder.
Even criminals have rights.

00:34:10.150 --> 00:34:12.450
And this is an unauthorized
human medical experiment,

00:34:12.590 --> 00:34:18.180
illegal under Cyber Law Article 42.
Penalty: 150 years.

00:34:22.070 --> 00:34:24.100
You're far too soft, Hasegawa.

00:34:25.030 --> 00:34:30.900
This city needs an iron
fist to restore order.

00:34:31.070 --> 00:34:37.540
In this case, the
ends justify the means.

00:34:37.870 --> 00:34:39.950
Once the President sees this test,

00:34:39.950 --> 00:34:43.300
we'll be able to destroy
every criminal in Oedo.

00:34:44.430 --> 00:34:46.780
But your test isn't finished yet.

00:34:47.630 --> 00:34:50.660
Preposterous!
Our weapon is clearly superior.

00:34:50.830 --> 00:34:54.060
Your hound spent the
entire time running for his life.

00:34:57.670 --> 00:34:59.340
Goggles, do you read me?

00:35:02.110 --> 00:35:06.060
You lost round one,
but the fight isn't over yet.

00:35:06.670 --> 00:35:10.290
It's time for round two.
You have ten minutes left.

00:35:12.670 --> 00:35:15.260
For once, I agree with you.

00:35:15.790 --> 00:35:18.660
I won't give up.

00:35:22.950 --> 00:35:25.940
Are you actually going to
go near that thing again?

00:35:26.470 --> 00:35:33.870
Those injuries will decrease
athletic performance by 70%.

00:35:33.870 --> 00:35:39.180
Just shut up and watch.
This is MY fight!

00:35:39.950 --> 00:35:43.220
He seems determined.
Better let him do it.

00:36:06.430 --> 00:36:10.620
Intermission is over.
Time for round two.

00:36:28.190 --> 00:36:31.100
Internal temperature is
over-limit, and rising.

00:36:31.790 --> 00:36:34.860
This may overload the
circulatory pumps.

00:36:35.950 --> 00:36:40.810
Don't worry.
My MOLCOS design is flawless!

00:36:50.470 --> 00:36:51.340
Damn!

00:37:48.270 --> 00:37:50.730
Where is he?

00:38:34.980 --> 00:38:36.010
What happened?

00:38:36.780 --> 00:38:40.560
I don't know! The central
control system has gone crazy!

00:38:43.660 --> 00:38:46.040
What's wrong, monster?

00:38:52.060 --> 00:38:54.090
varsus, do you read me?

00:38:54.580 --> 00:38:55.930
Affirmative.

00:38:57.280 --> 00:39:00.080
He's still going!

00:39:00.080 --> 00:39:01.630
He's quite impressive.

00:39:01.920 --> 00:39:06.670
Record this sound.

00:39:13.800 --> 00:39:16.360
Recording complete.

00:39:16.480 --> 00:39:21.190
Amplify and reproduce the sound
on the speaker in my collar.

00:39:21.320 --> 00:39:22.460
Affirmative.

00:39:35.960 --> 00:39:40.430
The echo! That frequency is
shorting out the control system!

00:39:40.560 --> 00:39:41.670
MOLCOS!

00:39:41.800 --> 00:39:44.590
It doesn't look so good
anymore, does it?

00:40:04.840 --> 00:40:07.400
Time for the final round!

00:40:36.960 --> 00:40:38.230
MOLCOS!

00:40:40.720 --> 00:40:44.070
The test isn't over yet!
Get up!

00:40:58.380 --> 00:41:01.250
MOLCOS!
Get up and kill him!

00:41:07.140 --> 00:41:09.850
Now it's just you and me.

00:41:11.380 --> 00:41:17.250
Your boy did okay for a while,
but he's kind of a mess now.

00:41:17.860 --> 00:41:20.570
Now it's your turn.

00:41:22.420 --> 00:41:28.250
I'll never forgive you
for bringing Sara into this.

00:41:30.380 --> 00:41:34.160
You'll die this time!
You can see your girlfriend in hell!

00:41:58.660 --> 00:42:02.690
It looks like your perfect
weapon had some problems.

00:42:03.300 --> 00:42:06.890
How tragic it must be, seeing
everything crumble like this.

00:42:07.220 --> 00:42:12.890
You can expect a subpoena
sometime in the next few days.

00:42:15.980 --> 00:42:20.890
Good work.
You won the match.

00:43:58.180 --> 00:44:05.970
Hiding my true feelings
from everyone.

00:44:10.140 --> 00:44:15.050
Never to see you anymore

00:44:15.580 --> 00:44:20.010
Has turned out to be so painful for me.

00:44:21.180 --> 00:44:26.450
Before time moves on without us

00:44:26.540 --> 00:44:30.930
And takes you away forever

00:44:32.180 --> 00:44:37.610
I just want to say I love you

00:44:37.740 --> 00:44:41.970
Ever so gently I whisper.

00:44:46.060 --> 00:44:51.450
Before time moves on without us

00:44:51.540 --> 00:44:55.970
And takes you away forever

00:44:57.100 --> 00:45:02.490
I just want to say I love you

00:45:02.580 --> 00:45:06.970
Ever so gently I whisper.

00:45:08.060 --> 00:45:10.690
Putting my trust and faith in you
